This note is not a second licence. It is here because two directories are
pictures rather than code, and a reader who finds them will wonder.

  docs/art/    One plate per version, painted once by tools/chronicle-art.sh
               through Cloudflare Workers AI and committed as an ordinary
               file. Machine-made from a prompt built out of the commit;
               nobody sat and drew one. A plate can be repainted.

  docs/faces/  One portrait per pilot, painted the same way and never again.
               A face is somebody's, in the sense that matters here rather
               than the sense a court would use: the manifest is the lock, no
               flag exists to overwrite one, and adding a flag is a rule
               change. If a pilot wants their face out of the book, that is
               their call and it needs no argument.

The rest of the media in media/ is hand-made and covered by the licence.
